{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0132jmk4j7bHRzxr23sBHhHd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Optimization Ideas (ranked by expected_impact × probability / complexity):**\n\n| # | Idea | Expected Impact | Probability | Complexity | Score |\n|---|------|----------------|-------------|------------|-------|\n| 1 | Warp-tiled intermediates buffer layout for GKR input eval | 50-100ms wall | High | Simple | **Best** |\n| 2 | Precompute/reuse monomial batch descriptors across MLE rounds | 10-15ms | High | Moderate | Medium |\n| 3 | Move compute_batch_s_poly to GPU | ~15ms | Medium | Moderate | Low |\n| 4 | Multi-stream Trace Commit RS expansion | 50-100ms | Low | Complex | Low (monolithic architecture blocks it) |\n| 5 | Reduce MLE Rounds per-AIR overhead via persistent kernel | 30-60ms | Low | Complex | Low |\n\n**Idea 1 wins clearly.** The GKR input eval kernel's intermediates buffer has a stride-65536 access pattern causing systematic L1/L2 cache misses. Reorganizing to a warp-tiled layout (stride-32) makes per-warp working set fit in L2 and partially in L1. The change is ~15 lines across 4 files with no algorithm change."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4582,"cache_read_input_tokens":150175,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4582},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da7aeca3-2690-42a7-b268-944d05bc2153","uuid":"4432f281-113c-457f-844c-c5736fa8a40d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0132jmk4j7bHRzxr23sBHhHd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RNQjQSz8nYnB2RaR8ydsjc","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-14-1430-warp-tiled-gkr-intermediates\n\nReorganize the GKR input evaluation GLOBAL-mode intermediates buffer from a thread-interleaved layout (stride = 65536) to a warp-tiled layout (stride = 32) to improve GPU cache locality. The `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel<true>` is the single largest GPU kernel at 464ms (19.5% of total GPU time), and its intermediates buffer accesses currently cause systematic L1 cache misses because consecutive DAG node accesses within a thread jump 65536 × 16 = 1MB apart. With warp-tiled layout, per-warp working set drops from ~100MB to ~50KB, fitting in L2 and partially in L1, for an estimated 1.3-1.5x kernel speedup translating to 50-100ms wall-time reduction on LogUp GKR.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4582,"cache_read_input_tokens":150175,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4582},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da7aeca3-2690-42a7-b268-944d05bc2153","uuid":"2051c69c-a909-4e45-ab62-94b8c5e6247e"}
