reduce 40K allocations to ~40, eliminating the per-matrix allocation/free overhead and improving memory pool behavior for subsequent phases.","+Reorganize the GKR input evaluation GLOBAL-mode intermediates buffer from a thread-interleaved layout (stride = 65536) to a warp-tiled layout (stride = 32) to improve GPU cache locality. The `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel<true>` is the single largest GPU kernel at 464ms (19.5% of total GPU time), and its intermediates buffer accesses currently cause systematic L1 cache misses because consecutive DAG node accesses within a thread jump 65536 × 16 = 1MB apart. With warp-tiled layout, per-warp working set drops from ~100MB to ~50KB, fitting in L2 and partially in L1, for an estimated 1.3-1.5x kernel speedup translating to 50-100ms wall-time reduction on LogUp GKR."]}],"originalFile":"# 2026-04-14-1200-bulk-alloc-mle-fold-buffers\n\nReplace per-matrix GPU buffer allocation in MLE sumcheck fold rounds with bulk pre-allocated arena buffers. Currently, each MLE round allocates ~2000 individual DeviceBuffers for fold output matrices (one per trace matrix for both mat_evals and sels), totaling ~40K cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync calls across ~20 rounds. This per-round allocation overhead causes MLE Rounds to reverse-scale at APC 300 (173ms vs 114ms at APC 0 despite 2x less work), contributing ~59ms of pure CUDA memory API overhead on the main thread. By allocating a single contiguous buffer per fold group per round, we reduce 40K allocations to ~40, eliminating the per-matrix allocation/free overhead and improving memory pool behavior for subsequent phases.\n"}}
