{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018uxubfX5dsyDMhqxqrwjqu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-14-1430-warp-tiled-gkr-intermediates\n2\t\n3\tReorganize the GKR input evaluation GLOBAL-mode intermediates buffer from a thread-interleaved layout (stride = 65536) to a warp-tiled layout (stride = 32) to improve GPU cache locality. The `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel<true>` is the single largest GPU kernel at 464ms (19.5% of total GPU time), and its intermediates buffer accesses currently cause systematic L1 cache misses because consecutive DAG node accesses within a thread jump 65536 × 16 = 1MB apart. With warp-tiled layout, per-warp working set drops from ~100MB to ~50KB, fitting in L2 and partially in L1, for an estimated 1.3-1.5x kernel speedup translating to 50-100ms wall-time reduction on LogUp GKR.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rnpmi6h3WD5rHK39B8jWDH","session_id":"da7aeca3-2690-42a7-b268-944d05bc2153","uuid":"3be72a8a-14f1-408f-92d3-4045bb06f346","timestamp":"2026-04-14T11:07:47.020Z"}
