{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019iEDqjnU9utgwaqqgG778u","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Warp-Tiled GKR Intermediates Buffer Layout\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tImprove GPU cache locality in the GKR input evaluation GLOBAL-mode kernel by reorganizing the intermediates buffer from a thread-interleaved layout to a warp-tiled layout. This targets the single largest GPU kernel (`evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel<true>`, 464ms total GPU time, 486 instances at APC 300) which currently suffers from systematic L1/L2 cache misses due to a stride-65536 access pattern in its DAG node cache.\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t### Call chain\n10\t\n11\t1. `log_gkr_input_evals()` at `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs:215` — orchestrates multi-stream dispatch\n12\t2. `process_gkr_input_air()` at `gkr_input.rs:100` — processes one AIR on one OS thread\n13\t3. `logup_gkr_input_eval()` FFI wrapper at `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` — safe Rust wrapper\n14\t4. `_logup_gkr_input_eval()` C launcher at `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu:216` — launches CUDA kernel\n15\t5. `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel<true>` at `gkr_input.cu:65` — the kernel itself\n16\t\n17\t### Current intermediates layout\n18\t\n19\tThe GLOBAL-mode intermediates buffer is allocated per-thread at `gkr_input.rs:308`:\n20\t```rust\n21\tintermediates: DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_intermediates_len),\n22\t// where max_intermediates_len = TASK_SIZE * max_buffer_size = 65536 * B\n23\t```\n24\t\n25\tIn the kernel (`gkr_input.cu:80-87`), each CUDA thread computes its pointer into the shared buffer:\n26\t```cpp\n27\tuint32_t task_offset = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;  // thread's global ID\n28\tuint32_t task_stride = gridDim.x * blockDim.x;                 // = 65536 (TASK_SIZE)\n29\tintermediates_ptr = (FpExt *)d_intermediates + task_offset;\n30\tintermediate_stride = task_stride;  // = 65536\n31\t```\n32\t\n33\tDAG nodes are accessed as `intermediates_ptr[node_idx * intermediate_stride]`, meaning:\n34\t- Thread `i` reads node `j` at address: `base + i + j * 65536`\n35\t- Within a warp (32 consecutive threads), all access the same node `j` at consecutive addresses → **coalesced** for a single node\n36\t- But within a single thread, consecutive nodes `j` and `j+1` are **65536 × 16 = 1MB apart** → every node-to-node access misses L1 and likely L2\n37\t\n38\t### Why this is slow\n39\t\n40\t- **Per-warp working set**: `buffer_size × 65536 × 16 bytes` ≈ 100 × 65536 × 16 ≈ **100MB** — far exceeds L1 (128KB) and L2 (72MB)\n41\t- **L1 hit rate**: ~0% (working set >> L1 capacity)\n42\t- **L2 hit rate**: ~72% (100MB vs 72MB L2) — 28% of accesses go to DRAM\n43\t- Each DAG evaluation reads/writes intermediates ~2× per node (read source + write result if buffered)\n44\t- With ~100 nodes per row and 65536 concurrent threads, this generates enormous memory traffic\n45\t\n46\t### Grid configuration\n47\t\n48\t- TASK_SIZE = 65536 = 2^16 (`gkr_input.cu:214`, `gkr_input.rs:27`)\n49\t- Block size = 256 threads\n50\t- Grid size = 256 blocks\n51\t- Total threads = 65536\n52\t- `num_rows_per_tile = ceil(height / 65536)` — each thread processes 1+ rows\n53\t\n54\t## Changes\n55\t\n56\t### 1. Add `buffer_size` parameter to CUDA kernel and launcher\n57\t\n58\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu`\n59\t\n60\tAdd `uint32_t buffer_size` parameter to `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel`:\n61\t\n62\t```cpp\n63\ttemplate <bool GLOBAL>\n64\t__global__ void evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel(\n65\t    FracExt *__restrict__ d_fracs,\n66\t    // ... existing params ...\n67\t    const uint32_t num_rows_per_tile,\n68\t    const uint32_t buffer_size  // NEW\n69\t)\n70\t```\n71\t\n72\tAdd `uint32_t buffer_size` parameter to `_logup_gkr_input_eval` launcher (`gkr_input.cu:216`), pass through to kernel call (`gkr_input.cu:234`, `gkr_input.cu:249`). For the `GLOBAL=false` template instantiation, `buffer_size` is unused but still passed (consistent signature).\n73\t\n74\t### 2. Change GLOBAL intermediates layout in kernel\n75\t\n76\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu`, lines 80-92\n77\t\n78\tReplace the current GLOBAL pointer setup:\n79\t\n80\t```cpp\n81\t// BEFORE:\n82\tuint32_t task_offset = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;\n83\tuint32_t task_stride = gridDim.x * blockDim.x;\n84\tif constexpr (GLOBAL) {\n85\t    intermediates_ptr = (FpExt *)d_intermediates + task_offset;\n86\t    intermediate_stride = task_stride;\n87\t}\n88\t```\n89\t\n90\tWith warp-tiled layout:\n91\t\n92\t```cpp\n93\t// AFTER:\n94\tuint32_t task_offset = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;\n95\tuint32_t task_stride = gridDim.x * blockDim.x;\n96\tconstexpr uint32_t WARP_SIZE = 32;\n97\tif constexpr (GLOBAL) {\n98\t    uint32_t warp_id = task_offset / WARP_SIZE;\n99\t    uint32_t lane_id = task_offset % WARP_SIZE;\n100\t    intermediates_ptr = (FpExt *)d_intermediates + warp_id * buffer_size * WARP_SIZE + lane_id;\n101\t    intermediate_stride = WARP_SIZE;\n102\t}\n103\t```\n104\t\n105\tThe `task_offset` and `task_stride` variables are unchanged — they're still used for the row-processing loop:\n106\t```cpp\n107\tuint32_t row = task_offset + j * task_stride;  // unchanged\n108\t```\n109\t\n110\tThe DAG evaluation helper (`evaluate_dag_entry_gkr`) and the inner loops access intermediates via `intermediates_ptr[node * intermediate_stride]`, which now reads:\n111\t- `base + warp_id * B * 32 + lane_id + node * 32`\n112\t- For a warp: 32 consecutive threads access `warp_id * B * 32 + [0..31] + node * 32` → coalesced (same as before)\n113\t- For a thread: consecutive nodes are `32 * 16 = 512 bytes` apart → **fits in L1 cache lines**\n114\t\n115\t### 3. Update Rust FFI binding\n116\t\n117\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n118\t\n119\tAdd `buffer_size: u32` to the `_logup_gkr_input_eval` extern declaration (around line 278). Update the safe wrapper `logup_gkr_input_eval()` to accept and pass `buffer_size`.\n120\t\n121\t### 4. Update Rust call site\n122\t\n123\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`, line 174\n124\t\n125\tPass `buffer_size as u32` to the `logup_gkr_input_eval()` call. The value is already available as `rules.inner.buffer_size` (line 158).\n126\t\n127\t## Memory Layout Comparison\n128\t\n129\t### Current (thread-interleaved, stride = 65536)\n130\t\n131\t```\n132\tMemory: [t0_n0, t1_n0, ..., t65535_n0, t0_n1, t1_n1, ..., t65535_n1, ...]\n133\t         |<---- 65536 elements ---->|  |<---- 65536 elements ---->|\n134\t```\n135\t\n136\tThread 0 accesses nodes at offsets: 0, 65536, 131072, ... (1MB apart)\n137\t\n138\t### Proposed (warp-tiled, stride = 32)\n139\t\n140\t```\n141\tMemory: [w0: t0_n0..t31_n0, t0_n1..t31_n1, ..., t0_nB..t31_nB] [w1: ...] [w2: ...] ...\n142\t         |<---- 32 * buffer_size elements per warp ---->|\n143\t```\n144\t\n145\tThread 0 accesses nodes at offsets: 0, 32, 64, ... (512 bytes apart)\n146\tPer-warp contiguous block: `buffer_size × 32 × 16` bytes ≈ **50KB** (for buffer_size=100)\n147\t\n148\t### Cache impact\n149\t\n150\t| Metric | Current | Proposed |\n151\t|--------|---------|----------|\n152\t| Inter-node stride per thread | 1MB (65536 × 16B) | 512B (32 × 16B) |\n153\t| Per-warp working set | ~100MB | ~50KB |\n154\t| L1 hit rate (128KB cache, ~8 warps/SM) | ~0% | ~30% |\n155\t| L2 hit rate (72MB cache) | ~72% | ~100% |\n156\t| Est. avg latency per intermediates access | ~284 cycles | ~146 cycles |\n157\t\n158\t## Invariants\n159\t\n160\t1. **Buffer capacity unchanged.** Total allocation remains `TASK_SIZE * buffer_size` FpExt elements. Only the mapping from (warp, node, lane) to memory address changes.\n161\t2. **No cross-thread intermediates access.** Each thread reads/writes only its own scratch region. The layout change doesn't affect data sharing.\n162\t3. **SCATTER mode (`GLOBAL=false`) unaffected.** Uses local stack array with stride 1. The `buffer_size` parameter is passed but unused.\n163\t4. **Row-processing loop unchanged.** `task_offset` and `task_stride` still govern which rows each thread processes.\n164\t5. **DAG evaluation semantics unchanged.** Same nodes, same operations, same results. Only the physical memory addresses change.\n165\t6. **Coalescing for same-node warp access preserved.** Threads 0..31 still access consecutive addresses for a given node (offset `[0..31]` within the warp tile).\n166\t7. **Output buffer unchanged.** Writes to `d_fracs` are independent of intermediates layout.\n167\t8. **Proof correctness preserved.** The kernel produces identical (p, q) fractional pairs for all AIRs.\n168\t\n169\t## Measurement Plan\n170\t\n171\t### Commands\n172\t\n173\t```bash\n174\t# In the powdr repo:\n175\tcd /home/georg/powdr/results/pairing\n176\t\n177\t# Build\n178\tcargo build --bin powdr_openvm_riscv -r --features \"metrics,cuda\"\n179\t\n180\t# APC 300 (primary target — run 3x for median)\n181\tRUST_LOG=info ./target/release/powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics apc300/metrics.json --recursion\n182\t\n183\t# APC 0 (regression check)\n184\tRUST_LOG=info ./target/release/powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics apc000/metrics.json --recursion\n185\t\n186\t# nsight profiling (APC 300 — verify kernel time reduction)\n187\tnsys profile --output nsys_apc300 --force-overwrite true --trace cuda,nvtx,osrt --sample none --stats true -- ./target/release/powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --recursion\n188\t```\n189\t\n190\t### Expected results\n191\t\n192\t- **LogUp GKR at APC 300**: 532ms → 450-480ms (10-15% improvement)\n193\t- **STARK excl trace at APC 300**: 1317ms → 1220-1270ms (50-100ms improvement)\n194\t- **APC 0 regression**: no change (single-threaded path with <100 AIRs)\n195\t- **nsight kernel sum**: `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel<true>` should drop from 464ms to 310-360ms total GPU time\n196\t\n197\t### Verification\n198\t\n199\t1. Proof verifies at all APC configs (0, 100, 300)\n200\t2. `spec.py` shows LogUp GKR improvement ≥ 30ms at APC 300\n201\t3. `nsys stats --report cuda_gpu_kern_sum` shows `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel<true>` speedup ≥ 1.2x\n202\t4. APC 0 STARK excl trace within ±20ms of before (no regression)\n203\t\n204\t## Rollback Criteria\n205\t\n206\t- Revert if STARK excl trace improvement at APC 300 < 30ms (below measurement noise threshold)\n207\t- Revert if APC 0 regresses by > 20ms\n208\t- Revert if any APC configuration fails proof verification\n209\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rnpmi6h3WD5rHK39B8jWDH","session_id":"da7aeca3-2690-42a7-b268-944d05bc2153","uuid":"db2ee251-9c41-4c3d-b00f-93d84af267cb","timestamp":"2026-04-14T11:07:47.174Z"}
