{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0154EvJ99kAHzZ7mhV9VBABe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UKYR3RSCKXVRgwMeWqTg7S","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","old_string":"Reorganize the GKR input evaluation GLOBAL-mode intermediates buffer from a thread-interleaved layout (stride = 65536) to a warp-tiled layout (stride = 32) to improve GPU cache locality. The `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel<true>` is the single largest GPU kernel at 464ms (19.5% of total GPU time), and its intermediates buffer accesses currently cause systematic L1 cache misses because consecutive DAG node accesses within a thread jump 65536 × 16 = 1MB apart. With warp-tiled layout, per-warp working set drops from ~100MB to ~50KB, fitting in L2 and partially in L1, for an estimated 1.3-1.5x kernel speedup translating to 50-100ms wall-time reduction on LogUp GKR.","new_string":"Reorganize the GKR input evaluation GLOBAL-mode intermediates buffer from a thread-interleaved layout (stride = 65536) to a warp-tiled layout (stride = 32) to improve GPU cache locality. The `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel<true>` is the single largest GPU kernel at 464ms (19.5% of total GPU time), and its intermediates buffer accesses currently cause systematic TLB misses and defeat hardware prefetching because consecutive DAG node accesses within a thread jump 65536 × 16 = 1MB apart. With warp-tiled layout, per-warp working set drops from ~100MB scattered to ~50KB contiguous, enabling hardware prefetch (stride 512B vs 1MB), reducing TLB pressure by ~8x, and improving L2 sector reuse, for an estimated 1.2-1.5x kernel speedup translating to 30-60ms wall-time reduction on LogUp GKR."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1013,"cache_read_input_tokens":165579,"cache_creation"